# license details.
#
# openi2pd: i2pd.tmpfiles.
#
# systemd-tmpfiles policy for the persistent state directory and for the
# runtime and log paths used by the service definitions. The packaged
# systemd unit also declares
# StateDirectory=/RuntimeDirectory=/LogsDirectory= for the same paths,
# so service startup does not depend on tmpfiles having run.
#
# The 0700 mode is a security requirement, not a cosmetic default: the
# state directory holds the router identity keys and the mode-0600 TUI
# socket, and the log directory must not be readable by other local
# accounts. A `d` line also re-applies mode and ownership to an existing
# directory on every run, so an administrator who deliberately widens
# the log directory needs a local drop-in; debian/postinst only
# preserves custom modes during package upgrade.
#
# These entries matter on a systemd host. A non-systemd host never runs
# systemd-tmpfiles, and the maintainer script creates the same three
# paths.

d /var/lib/i2pd 0700 i2pd i2pd -
d /var/log/i2pd 0700 i2pd i2pd -
d /run/i2pd 0700 i2pd i2pd -
